                        eg : https://github.com/kktestcgnt/pyleafs.git

        ->In Branch specifier fill with below
                    */main

        ->click ok to create a pipeline
        ->click on job created and then click on build now

********************************************************************
I am having two windows base os systems(System-1 and System-2). In System-1 i am having python file in D drive that needs to be executed. 
In System-2 i want to install jenkins, i need step by step how to install in System-2 After installing the jenkins in System-2 ,
create a jenkins pipline that runs the python file which is there in System-1. need the steps how to acheive this through jenkins node.
********************************************************************
STEP-1
System-2 (Windows)
→ Jenkins Controller (UI + Pipeline)

System-1 (Windows)
→ Jenkins Agent
→ Has Python installed
→ Has your Python file in D:\scripts\test.py

On both System-1 & System-2:

Download Java 17 (LTS)
https://adoptium.net

Install → next → next.

Verify:
edit environtment variables : JAVA_HOME = C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-21\bin\java.exe
cmd> java -version


STEP 2: Install Jenkins on System-2 (Controller)
1. Download Jenkins (Windows)

https://www.jenkins.io/download/

Choose:

Windows Installer (.msi)

2. Install Jenkins

Run .msi

Default port: 8080

Service account: Local System (recommended)

Finish install

3. Unlock Jenkins

Open browser:

http://localhost:8080


Password location:

C:\Program Files\Jenkins\secrets\initialAdminPassword


Paste password → Install Suggested Plugins

4. Create admin user

Done 🎉 Jenkins is up.

STEP 3: Create Jenkins Agent (Node) on System-2
1. Go to Jenkins Dashboard →

Manage Jenkins → Nodes → New Node

2. Node configuration
Field	Value
Node name	windows-agent-1
Type	Permanent Agent
3. Node details
Setting	Value
Remote root directory	C:\jenkins_agent
Labels	win-agent
Usage	Only build jobs with label expressions
Launch method	Launch agent by connecting it to the controller
Availability	Keep this agent online

Save.

note: 
for agent download in system-1 use below steps 
cmd>mkdir C:\jenkins_agent
cmd>cd jenkins_agent
cmd>curl.exe -sO http://localhost:8080/jnlpJars/agent.jar
                        or
browser> http://localhost:8080/jnlpJars/agent.jar
cmd>java -jar agent.jar -url http://localhost:8080/ -secret 567b0f5712882f8a6c9f37325f952a7a0f83b99f9e42b04b2b0d40b9 -name "windows-agent-1" -webSocket -workDir "C:\jenkins_agent"
response:
INFO: Connecting to http://192.168.1.20:8080/
INFO: Handshaking
INFO: Connected

if not connected : check below ones
In this file C:\Program Files\Jenkins\jenkins.xml 
for this line in jenkins.xml 
<arguments>-Xrs -Xmx256m -Dhudson.lifecycle=hudson.lifecycle.WindowsServiceLifecycle -jar "C:\Program Files\Jenkins\jenkins.war" --httpPort=8080 --webroot="%ProgramData%\Jenkins\war"</arguments>
{httpListenAddress=0.0.0.0 is not there in above line after adding it looks like}
<arguments>-Xrs -Xmx256m -Dhudson.lifecycle=hudson.lifecycle.WindowsServiceLifecycle -jar "C:\Program Files\Jenkins\jenkins.war" --httpListenAddress=0.0.0.0 --httpPort=8080 --webroot="%ProgramData%\Jenkins\war"</arguments>

note:
Open firewall (don’t skip)

On System-2:

Windows Defender Firewall

Advanced settings

Inbound Rules → New Rule

Port → TCP → 8080 → Allow

✅ Step-6.1: Create a new Pipeline job

On System-2 Jenkins UI:

Open browser → http://localhost:8080

Click New Item

Enter name:

run-python-from-system1


Select Pipeline

Click OK

groovy file:
pipeline {
    agent {
        label 'windows-agent-1'
    }

    stages {
        stage('Check Java & Python') {
            steps {
                bat '''
                java -version
                python --version
                '''
            }
        }

        stage('Run Python File on System-1') {
            steps {
                bat '''
                python D:\Preparations\Jenkins_remote_python_execution\one.py
                '''
            }
        }
    }
}


